{"duration_api_ms":256029,"stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"4daee34f-aa7f-4fdf-b8aa-f60d9ebbba8e","total_cost_usd":1.848376,"usage":{"input_tokens":66,"cache_creation_input_tokens":103476,"cache_read_input_tokens":2604920,"output_tokens":24966,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":7698},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":103476,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1085,"cache_read_input_tokens":106945,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2511,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2511},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-opus-5-5":{"inputTokens":66,"outputTokens":24966,"cacheReadInputTokens":2604920,"cacheCreationInputTokens":103476,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":1.848376,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":128000,"thinkingTokens":7698,"canonicalModel":"claude-opus-5-5","provider":"firstParty","costBasis":"list"}},"permission_denials":[{"tool_name":"Bash","tool_use_id":"toolu_01XeoxpbVcPT8AMCkNCW1fEn","tool_input":{"command":"env | grep -i e2e; curl -s -o /dev/null -w \"%{http_code}\\n\" http://localhost:5080/ ; lsof -iTCP -sTCP:LISTEN -n -P 2>/dev/null | grep -i \"dotnet\\|java\" | head","description":"Check E2E env vars and running shops"}},{"tool_name":"Bash","tool_use_id":"toolu_01CsUuu9qtsqs94fx2xSaphP","tool_input":{"command":"printenv E2E_BASE_URL; echo \"---\"; curl -s -o /dev/null -w \"%{http_code}\\n\" http://localhost:5080/","description":"Check E2E base URL and whether shop runs"}},{"tool_name":"Bash","tool_use_id":"toolu_01WpNBjQBk9uT3L8TTWhgT3G","tool_input":{"command":"cd /Users/christoph/Privat/domain-centric-architecture/dca-ecommerce-sample-dotnet; sed -i '' '/^using System.Globalization;$/d' tests/DcaShop.IntegrationTests/ProviderPaymentTest.cs; export PATH=$HOME/.dotnet:$PATH; dotnet build 2>&1 | grep -E \"error|Warn|warn|Build succeeded\" | sort -u | head -20","timeout":400000,"description":"Build the solution after adding tests"}},{"tool_name":"Bash","tool_use_id":"toolu_01P4bz3F5S75Qzg5jwr2aF1S","tool_input":{"command":"head -30 .agents/factory/decisions/product-slider-01.md; find .. -path '*factory-run/templates/decision.md.tmpl' 2>/dev/null | head -1 | xargs cat","description":"Read decision record format"}}],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","fast_mode_disabled_reason":"sdk_opt_in_required","subagent_stats":{"spawned":0,"requested":{"background":0,"foreground":0,"unset":0},"started_in_background":0,"max_depth":0,"spawned_by_subagents":0,"completed":0,"failed":0,"killed":{"parent":0,"user":0,"system":0},"refused":{"depth_limit":0,"concurrency_limit":0,"budget":0},"by_type":{}},"is_error":false,"num_turns":43,"subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"The test stage for `pay-through-the-provider` is only partly done. Two of the three criteria have red tests. The happy path, `authorized-payment-moves-to-review`, has no test yet and is waiting on your decision.\n\n**Why the happy path is blocked.** The plan wants a Playwright test in which the shop pays through the test's WireMock.Net stub. Three things stop that:\n- The browser suite runs against a shop someone else started, and the test can't point that shop at its own stub. The plan's idea of skipping the test when the stub address isn't set doesn't work: the story gate treats a skipped test as a failure.\n- If that shop *is* started with a provider address, the real provider replaces the stand-in. The three existing checkout browser tests would then be refused as \"unavailable\" whenever this test's stub isn't running. I'm not allowed to change those tests, because the plan lists no changed tests.\n- No basket reaches 20.00 EUR. Every seeded price and shipping cost ends in .99. Creating a 20.00 product needs a staff token, and a browser test against a running shop has no way to get one.\n\n**The decision** is in `.agents/factory/decisions/pay-through-the-provider-01.md`, with three options:\n- **a (recommended):** one shared stub for the whole browser suite that approves every payment, plus two environment variables: the stub's address and an out-of-band staff token. The existing tests stay unchanged, but the worker environment and CI have to supply both.\n- **b:** re-plan the happy path as an integration test.\n- **c:** offer the stand-in alongside the real provider instead of replacing it.\n\n**What's written:**\n- `tests/DcaShop.IntegrationTests/ProviderPaymentTest.cs` — the shop runs in-process pointed at a WireMock.Net stub, and the customer pays over `POST /checkout/payment`.\n  - Mapped: the refusal (402) and the slow provider (5 s delay, also asserting the answer comes back in under 4 s).\n  - Not mapped, covering other answers from the provider: approval with a reference (one request for 9.99 EUR, then the review step), a 500, a 201 with no reference, and a provider that can't be reached.\n  - All six fail on their assertions. The shop doesn't read the provider address yet, so the stand-in takes every payment.\n- `tests/DcaShop.UnitTests/Checkout/SubmitPaymentUseCaseTest.cs` — two new unit tests: a refusal raises `PaymentInitiationFailedException`, an unreachable provider raises `PaymentProviderUnavailableException`, and neither changes the session. Both are red on `Assert.ThrowsAsync`. The four existing tests still pass and none of their lines changed.\n- The only production change is a stub: `PaymentResult.Refused` and `PaymentResult.Unavailable` in `IPaymentProvider.cs` throw `NotImplementedException`.\n- `tasks/pay-through-the-provider/tests.md` has the mapping table, a `## needs-human` section and the notes.\n\nThe solution compiles, `dotnet format` has been applied, and no scratch tests are left. I didn't run any other stage and committed nothing.","ttft_ms":2957,"type":"result","duration_ms":295488,"uuid":"3f93f1dd-9aec-4a8a-bf00-3526f4bdefbe","ttft_stream_ms":1816,"time_to_request_ms":62,"first_content_frame_ms":1816,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0}
